        <SPEC-RELATION-TYPE IDENTIFIER="SRT-VERIFIES" LONG-NAME="verifies" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00" DESC="Declared with zero instances in Phase 1. The right leg of the V adds SPEC-RELATION elements of this type from test-case spec-objects to requirement spec-objects, with no change to this type model."/>
      </SPEC-TYPES>
      <SPEC-OBJECTS>
        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_277a09a5-8ca2-5f12-883b-4b3829bd4258" LONG-NAME="1 Scope" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="1">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-NUMBER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="Scope">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>This document specifies the system-layer requirements for an Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system for a passenger car. The system is of <xhtml:strong>FSRA type</xhtml:strong> (full speed range adaptive cruise control) as classified by ISO 15622:2018 cl. 5.1 Table 1: it has no manual clutch dependency, it operates down to standstill, it holds the subject vehicle stationary by automatic brake control, and it resumes from standstill.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>The system controls the <xhtml:strong>longitudinal</xhtml:strong> motion of the subject vehicle only. It adjusts vehicle speed to a driver-set speed, or to the speed required to keep a selected time gap to a target vehicle, whichever is lower. It commands the brake actuator and the powertrain actuator, and it presents its state to the driver.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>What this document specifies</xhtml:strong>
                  </xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:ul>
                    <xhtml:li>The operating states of the ACC system and every transition between them.</xhtml:li>
                    <xhtml:li>The nominal control behaviour: mode arbitration, target vehicle selection, standstill handling and resume.</xhtml:li>
                    <xhtml:li>The numeric envelopes of vehicle motion: time gap, clearance, deceleration, jerk, acceleration and speed limits.</xhtml:li>
                    <xhtml:li>The response of the system in defined driving scenarios taken from the Euro NCAP Assisted Driving protocol.</xhtml:li>
                    <xhtml:li>The behaviour of the system when forward sensing, the vehicle bus or the actuators fail, and the limits that bound the authority of the system.</xhtml:li>
                    <xhtml:li>For every requirement: an attribute set that makes the requirement traceable and verifiable, including the signal to log and the provenance of every number.</xhtml:li>
                  </xhtml:ul>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>Layer</xhtml:strong>
                  </xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>This is the <xhtml:strong>system requirements</xhtml:strong> layer of the development V, corresponding to Automotive SPICE PAM 4.0 process <xhtml:strong>SYS.2 (System Requirements Analysis)</xhtml:strong>. Its counterpart on the right leg of the V is the system test specification (SYS.5), which is not part of this document. Requirements here state <xhtml:em>what</xhtml:em> the system does, never <xhtml:em>how</xhtml:em> it is implemented.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>What this document deliberately excludes</xhtml:strong>
                  </xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:table>
                    <xhtml:thead>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:th>Excluded</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>Where it belongs</xhtml:th>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:thead>
                    <xhtml:tbody>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>ISO 26262 in any form</xhtml:strong> — ASIL assignment, hazard analysis, safety case, technical safety requirements as a distinct class</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Out of project scope by fixed decision. Clause 7 of this document contains ordinary system requirements about safe behaviour, and nothing else</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Lateral control, lane centring, steering intervention</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>A separate function. ACC here is longitudinal only</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Autonomous emergency braking (AEB) behaviour</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>A separate system. This document specifies only how ACC yields the shared brake actuator to it (ACC-SYS-SAF-041)</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Stakeholder requirements and the item definition</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Assumed upstream (SYS.1); not produced here</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Software-unit and hardware decomposition, system architecture</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Downstream (SYS.3 and below)</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Test cases, test procedures, pass/fail criteria beyond what each requirement states</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The system test specification (SYS.5). The <xhtml:code>verified_by</xhtml:code> attribute of every requirement is deliberately empty in this revision</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Vehicle owner-manual content, homologation and type approval</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Out of scope, although ISO 15622:2018 cl. 5.1 requires the deceleration capability to be stated in the owner's manual</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:tbody>
                  </xhtml:table>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>Reading the verification tags</xhtml:strong>
                  </xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>Every requirement carries a <xhtml:code>verification_tag</xhtml:code> recording how well the numbers in it are sourced. The vocabulary is defined in clause 3.4 and in Annex B. One value deserves attention on first reading: <xhtml:strong>`UNVERIFIED-2018`</xhtml:strong> marks a requirement whose number is an <xhtml:em>engineering assumption</xhtml:em>, because the clause exists in ISO 15622:2018 but its value could only be read from a superseded edition. Those requirements are collected in the assumptions register of clause 3.4 and their bounds are drawn dashed and labelled on figures F4 and F6.</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-SECTION-BODY</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
          </VALUES>
          <TYPE>
            <SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>ST-ACC-SECTION</SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>
          </TYPE>
        </SPEC-OBJECT>
        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_419780b2-a92c-5e59-9013-bfe986f6d717" LONG-NAME="2 References" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="2">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-NUMBER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="References">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>2.1 Normative references</xhtml:strong>
                  </xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>The following documents are referred to in the requirement text of clauses 5, 6 and 7 in such a way that some or all of their content constitutes requirements of this document.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:table>
                    <xhtml:thead>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:th>Reference</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>Title / edition</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>Source label</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>URL</xhtml:th>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:thead>
                    <xhtml:tbody>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>ISO 15622:2018</xhtml:strong>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Intelligent transport systems — Adaptive cruise control systems — Performance requirements and test procedures. Third edition. Prepared by ISO/TC 204. Cancels and replaces ISO 15622:2010 and ISO 22179:2009</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Primary</xhtml:strong> for the publisher-hosted preview, which reaches cl. 6.2.3; <xhtml:strong>secondary or unverified</xhtml:strong> beyond that point</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://www.iso.org/standard/71515.html</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Euro NCAP AD v2.2 (2024-09)</xhtml:strong>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Assisted Driving Highway Assist Test &amp; Assessment Protocol, version 2.2, September 2024</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Primary</xhtml:strong> (official protocol PDF)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://cdn.euroncap.com/cars/assets/euro_ncap_ad_test_and_assessment_protocol_v22_71187c1b5e.pdf</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:tbody>
                  </xhtml:table>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>Edition caveat on ISO 15622:2018.</xhtml:strong> The publisher-hosted official preview carries the full table of contents, clause 3 terms, clause 4 symbols, clause 5.1 Table 1 classification, cl. 6.1, cl. 6.2.1 and cl. 6.2.3.1, then truncates in cl. 6.2.3. Clauses 6.2.4 ("Go" transition), 6.3 (driver interface), 6.4 (operational limits), 6.5 (activation of brake lights), 6.6 (failure reactions), clause 7 (test procedures) and Annex A are <xhtml:strong>not readable from any primary source retrieved for this project</xhtml:strong>. Every requirement that depends on those clauses is tagged <xhtml:code>UNVERIFIED-2018</xhtml:code> or <xhtml:code>DERIVED</xhtml:code> and appears in the assumptions register of clause 3.4.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>Baseline caveat on Euro NCAP.</xhtml:strong> v2.2 (2024-09) is the <xhtml:em>fixed</xhtml:em> scenario-parameter baseline of this project. It has been superseded: the current protocol is Assisted Driving Highway &amp; Interurban Assist Systems v1.1 (2025-10), which delegates the ACC test procedures to a separate "Vehicle Assistance protocol" that was not retrieved. Where the newer protocol is known to differ, the difference is stated in the rationale of the affected requirement — see ACC-SYS-PRF-061.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>2.2 Informative references</xhtml:strong>
                  </xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:table>
                    <xhtml:thead>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:th>Reference</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>What it is used for</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>Source label</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>URL</xhtml:th>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:thead>
                    <xhtml:tbody>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2010</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Second edition. Source of the cl. 6.4 operational limits used as <xhtml:code>UNVERIFIED-2018</xhtml:code> assumptions (deceleration, jerk, acceleration, minimum set speed)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Secondary</xhtml:strong> — read from an unauthorised full-text copy; corroborated, never treated as the standard</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://www.iso.org/standard/50024.html</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO/DIS 15622 (1999)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Draft international standard, ISO/TC 204/WG 14 N143.17, 1999-07-19. Source of the 100 ms brake-light timing; evidence that cl. 6.4 values move between drafts (it set 3,0 m/s², relaxed to 3,5 m/s² by publication)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Primary for that draft</xhtml:strong>, superseded for the published editions</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://www.oocities.org/hyoungjin2001/AVS/ACC.pdf</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2002</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>First edition. Evidence that the minimum time gap changed across editions (1 s in 2002, 0,8 s from 2010)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Primary</xhtml:strong> (publisher-hosted preview of the superseded edition)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://www.iso.org/standard/27834.html</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>EARS — Easy Approach to Requirements Syntax</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The six requirement patterns used by the <xhtml:code>ears_pattern</xhtml:code> attribute. Canonical publication by the co-author of the method</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Primary</xhtml:strong>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://alistairmavin.com/ears/</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>INCOSE Guide for Writing Requirements (GtWR)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The <xhtml:code>Rxx</xhtml:code> requirement-writing rules cited in the rationale of individual requirements and enforced by the build. Named by Automotive SPICE PAM 4.0 SYS.2.BP1 note 01 as a source of defined requirement characteristics</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Secondary</xhtml:strong> — the official INCOSE summary sheet returned HTTP 403 and could not be retrieved, so rule texts come from a tool-vendor guide quoting the GtWR. No rule <xhtml:em>count</xhtml:em> is stated anywhere in this document, deliberately</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://www.incose.org/</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Automotive SPICE PAM 4.0</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Process reference for SYS.2. Output information item <xhtml:code>17-54 Requirement attribute</xhtml:code> justifies the attribute schema of Annex B; SYS.2.BP1 note 02 justifies keeping verification criteria inside the requirement text rather than in a separate acceptance-criteria field</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Secondary</xhtml:strong> (accredited assessor provider summary of the paywalled VDA QMC publication)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://www.automotivespice.com/</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Euro NCAP AD v1.1 (2025-10)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Current protocol; noted for staleness tracking only, not used as a parameter source</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Primary</xhtml:strong>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://cdn.euroncap.com/cars/assets/euro_ncap_protocol_assisted_driving_v11_a6bfe1b5f2.pdf</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>OMG ReqIF 1.2</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Interchange format of the machine-readable export of this document. Namespace <xhtml:code>http://www.omg.org/spec/ReqIF/20110401/reqif.xsd</xhtml:code>. The schema tree is vendored at <xhtml:code>Reqs/export/schema/</xhtml:code>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:strong>Primary</xhtml:strong>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>https://www.omg.org/spec/ReqIF/</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:tbody>
                  </xhtml:table>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>2.3 Sources deliberately not used</xhtml:strong>
                  </xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:table>
                    <xhtml:thead>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:th>Not used</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>Why</xhtml:th>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:thead>
                    <xhtml:tbody>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>UN Regulation No. 79</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Governs steering equipment and automatically commanded steering functions. Not a longitudinal ACC instrument</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>UN Regulation No. 157 (ALKS)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Covers automated lane keeping systems. Borrowing its deceleration thresholds into an ACC requirement would be a category error</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>NHTSA / FMVSS</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>There is no FMVSS for ACC and no NHTSA ACC performance test procedure. The NHTSA ACC work is human-factors research; the 2024 AEB final rule covers AEB, not ACC. Any claim that NHTSA specifies ACC numbers is unsupported</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 26262 (all parts)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Out of scope by fixed project decision — see clause 1</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:tbody>
                  </xhtml:table>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-SECTION-BODY</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
          </VALUES>
          <TYPE>
            <SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>ST-ACC-SECTION</SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>
          </TYPE>
        </SPEC-OBJECT>
        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_d6a7b1af-3007-52d2-9881-df91bc7ded5b" LONG-NAME="3 Terms, definitions, symbols and assumptions" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="3">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-NUMBER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="Terms, definitions, symbols and assumptions">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>
                    <xhtml:strong>3.1 Terms and definitions</xhtml:strong>
                  </xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:p>Every term used in a requirement statement of clauses 5, 6 and 7 is defined here. The build fails if a requirement statement uses a controlled term that is absent from this table (INCOSE <xhtml:code>R4</xhtml:code>, "define terms"). Where ISO 15622:2018 defines the term, its clause is given and the definition follows the standard; the remaining terms are project definitions, marked <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:table>
                    <xhtml:thead>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:th>Term</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>Clause</xhtml:th>
                        <xhtml:th>Definition</xhtml:th>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:thead>
                    <xhtml:tbody>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>subject vehicle</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The vehicle in which the ACC system specified by this document is installed and whose longitudinal motion it controls</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>target vehicle</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3.13</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The forward vehicle that the ACC system has selected to follow</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>forward vehicle</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>A vehicle ahead of the subject vehicle and in the same lane, whether or not it is currently selected as the target vehicle</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>clearance</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The bumper-to-bumper longitudinal distance between the subject vehicle and the vehicle ahead of it</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>time gap</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The clearance divided by the speed of the subject vehicle, expressed in seconds</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>time gap setting</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>One of the discrete time gap values the driver may select; the ACC system regulates towards the selected setting</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>set speed</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 4</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The speed selected by the driver, denoted v_set, that the ACC system maintains when no target vehicle constrains it</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>speed control</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3.12.2</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The control sub-state in which the ACC system regulates the subject vehicle to the set speed</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>following control</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3.12.5</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The control sub-state in which the ACC system regulates the clearance or time gap to the target vehicle</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>hold state</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3.12.6</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The state of an FSRA-type system in which automatic brake control keeps the subject vehicle stationary; realised in this document as the Active-Hold state</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>standstill</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The condition in which the speed of the subject vehicle is zero</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>steady-state conditions</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 6.2.3.1</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Conditions in which the speeds of the subject vehicle and the target vehicle are constant and the clearance is settled, so that the regulated time gap can be measured</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>operating speed range</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The subject vehicle speed interval over which the ACC system controls longitudinal motion, from standstill to the maximum set speed of ACC-SYS-PRF-041</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>stationary object</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3.14</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>An object that is not moving along the centreline of the subject vehicle</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>stationary vehicle</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>A vehicle that is a stationary object</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>slow moving object</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 3.15</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>An object moving along the centreline of the subject vehicle at less than MAX(1,0 m/s, 10 % of the subject vehicle speed)</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>lane change</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Euro NCAP AD v2.2 (2024-09)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>A full lateral transfer of a vehicle between adjacent lanes, with a 3,5 m lateral offset in the test scenarios of this document</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>time to collision</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Euro NCAP AD v2.2 (2024-09)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The clearance divided by the relative closing speed, evaluated at the reference instant of a scenario</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>forward-sensing function</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The function inside the system boundary of figure F1 that detects and tracks forward vehicles by fusing radar and camera data</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>target detected status</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The binary indication of whether the ACC system currently has a target vehicle</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>forward-sensing health signal</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The internal signal reporting the availability and plausibility of the forward-sensing function</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>vehicle bus health signal</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The internal signal reporting whether the vehicle bus signals used for longitudinal control are being updated</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>actuation health signal</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The internal signal reporting whether the brake actuator and the powertrain actuator are delivering the commanded longitudinal acceleration</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>vehicle bus signal</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>A signal received by the ACC system from the vehicle network, such as wheel speed, yaw rate, pedal position, brake switch or ignition status</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>longitudinal acceleration</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The acceleration of the subject vehicle along its own centreline, positive forwards; a deceleration is a negative longitudinal acceleration and is stated in this document as a positive magnitude</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>commanded longitudinal acceleration</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The longitudinal acceleration that the ACC system requests of the brake actuator and the powertrain actuator</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>automatic brake control</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 5.1</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Brake actuation commanded by the ACC system rather than by the driver</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>automatic service braking</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Automatic brake control that produces a deceleration of the subject vehicle by the service brake</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>brake lights</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>ISO/DIS 15622 (1999) cl. 6.5</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The rear stop lamps of the subject vehicle</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>powertrain torque</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The propulsion torque delivered at the driven wheels of the subject vehicle</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>accelerator pedal</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The driver control whose position requests powertrain torque</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>brake pedal</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The driver control whose actuation requests service braking</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>set switch</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The driver control that activates the ACC system and adopts the current speed as the set speed</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>resume switch</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The driver control that commands a resume from the Active-Hold state</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>cancel switch</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The driver control that deactivates the ACC system to the Standby state</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>ignition</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The vehicle power state that enables or disables the ACC system</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>driver</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The person in the driving seat of the subject vehicle</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>hands-off condition</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Euro NCAP AD v2.2 (2024-09)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The condition in which the driver is not detected as holding the steering wheel</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>takeover warning escalation</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>Euro NCAP AD v2.2 (2024-09)</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The staged sequence of warnings that requests the driver to resume manual control</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>autonomous emergency braking system</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The separate system, outside the ACC system boundary of figure F1, that commands the shared brake actuator to avoid or mitigate a collision</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>ACC state</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The current operating state of the ACC system, one of the seven states of ACC-SYS-FUN-001</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Off</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The state in which the ACC system is not powered and controls nothing</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Standby</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The state in which the ACC system is powered, controls nothing, and is available for activation</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Active-Cruise</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The active state in which the ACC system is in speed control</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Active-Follow</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The active state in which the ACC system is in following control</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Active-Hold</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The active state in which the ACC system holds the subject vehicle at standstill by automatic brake control; the realisation of the ISO 15622:2018 hold state</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Driver-Override</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The state in which driver accelerator input takes precedence over the powertrain request of the ACC system</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                      <xhtml:tr>
                        <xhtml:td>Degraded-Fault</xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>
                          <xhtml:em>(project)</xhtml:em>
                        </xhtml:td>
                        <xhtml:td>The state the ACC system enters when it has detected a fault that prevents it from meeting the requirements of clauses 5 and 6</xhtml:td>
                      </xhtml:tr>
                    </xhtml:tbody>
                  </xhtml:table>
