        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_a8c26774-94c7-58fc-b541-49498a19225a" LONG-NAME="6 Performance requirements" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="6">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-NUMBER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="Performance requirements">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>This clause carries 12 requirements with identifiers ACC-SYS-PRF-###, ordered by identifier and grouped into 4 sub-clauses that follow the identifier allocation blocks.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:object data="figures/F3-clearance-geometry.svg" type="image/svg+xml" width="1120" height="700">
                    <xhtml:p>Figure F3 — Time gap and clearance geometry. Clearance and time gap geometry for following control, with the desired clearance relation MAX(c_min, tau times v), the c_min floor at low speed and an inset of desired clearance against subject vehicle speed showing the knee at v = c_min / tau.</xhtml:p>
                  </xhtml:object>
                  <xhtml:object data="figures/F4-follow-brake-trace.svg" type="image/svg+xml" width="1120" height="760">
                    <xhtml:p>Figure F4 — Annotated follow-and-brake trace. Two-panel time-aligned trace of a braking-target event: steady following, lead braking at 4 m/s², subject deceleration, and clearance re-establishment. The lower panel carries the deceleration and jerk bounds, drawn in the unverified-assumption style because both values are UNVERIFIED-2018.</xhtml:p>
                  </xhtml:object>
                  <xhtml:object data="figures/F5-cutin-cutout-geometry.svg" type="image/svg+xml" width="1120" height="800">
                    <xhtml:p>Figure F5 — Cut-in and cut-out geometry. Euro NCAP AD v2.2 (2024-09) cut-in and cut-out geometry, with the lateral offset, the lateral acceleration and lane-change length parameter sets, the turn radii, the speed pairs and the reference time-to-collision instants.</xhtml:p>
                  </xhtml:object>
                  <xhtml:object data="figures/F6-operating-envelope.svg" type="image/svg+xml" width="1120" height="720">
                    <xhtml:p>Figure F6 — Operating envelope. Permissible operating region in the subject vehicle speed against longitudinal acceleration plane. Every bound is annotated with its verification tag; UNVERIFIED-2018 bounds are dashed and carry the literal tag text.</xhtml:p>
                  </xhtml:object>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-SECTION-BODY</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
