        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_223cabd8-ac5d-5905-b645-a3f29e859382" LONG-NAME="7 Safety and fault-handling requirements" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="7">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-NUMBER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="Safety and fault-handling requirements">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SECTION-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>This clause carries 12 requirements with identifiers ACC-SYS-SAF-###, ordered by identifier and grouped into 4 sub-clauses that follow the identifier allocation blocks.</xhtml:p>
                  <xhtml:object data="figures/F1-system-boundary.svg" type="image/svg+xml" width="1120" height="700">
                    <xhtml:p>Figure F1 — System boundary block diagram. ACC system boundary. Inside the boundary: forward-sensing fusion, target selection, longitudinal control law, state manager, fault manager and HMI arbitration. Crossing the boundary: radar and camera inputs, vehicle bus inputs, HMI inputs, and commands to the brake actuator, the powertrain actuator, the brake-light control and the HMI display. Outside: the driver, the target vehicle and the autonomous emergency braking system, which shares the brake actuator.</xhtml:p>
                  </xhtml:object>
                  <xhtml:object data="figures/F2-state-machine.svg" type="image/svg+xml" width="1120" height="760">
                    <xhtml:p>Figure F2 — ACC state machine. The seven ACC operating states and every transition between them. Each arc carries its trigger and the identifier of the requirement that specifies it. Nominal arcs are drawn in the nominal accent, fault arcs in the fault accent.</xhtml:p>
                  </xhtml:object>
                  <xhtml:object data="figures/F4-follow-brake-trace.svg" type="image/svg+xml" width="1120" height="760">
                    <xhtml:p>Figure F4 — Annotated follow-and-brake trace. Two-panel time-aligned trace of a braking-target event: steady following, lead braking at 4 m/s², subject deceleration, and clearance re-establishment. The lower panel carries the deceleration and jerk bounds, drawn in the unverified-assumption style because both values are UNVERIFIED-2018.</xhtml:p>
                  </xhtml:object>
                  <xhtml:object data="figures/F6-operating-envelope.svg" type="image/svg+xml" width="1120" height="720">
                    <xhtml:p>Figure F6 — Operating envelope. Permissible operating region in the subject vehicle speed against longitudinal acceleration plane. Every bound is annotated with its verification tag; UNVERIFIED-2018 bounds are dashed and carry the literal tag text.</xhtml:p>
                  </xhtml:object>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-SECTION-BODY</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
          </VALUES>
          <TYPE>
            <SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>ST-ACC-SECTION</SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>
          </TYPE>
        </SPEC-OBJECT>
