        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_b0cc11a9-6ff3-53f6-841f-4c92a674d9d9" LONG-NAME="ACC-SYS-FUN-042" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ACC-SYS-FUN-042">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-ID</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="Deactivation to Standby on driver cancel command">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-CHAPTER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-CH-FUNCTIONAL-HMI</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>While the ACC system is in the Active-Cruise state, the Active-Follow state or the Active-Hold state, when the driver depresses the brake pedal or operates the cancel switch, the ACC system shall enter the Standby state.</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-TEXT</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-EARS-PATTERN</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-EARS-COMPLEX</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-SYSTEM-STATES</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-CRUISE</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-FOLLOW</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-HOLD</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-STANDBY</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 6.3.1 places driver braking precedence over ACC braking in the standard; the clause is past the truncation point of the publisher-hosted preview and was read from the ISO/TC 204 community extract, hence VERIFIED-SECONDARY. The cancel switch is the second deactivation trigger and is project-owned. Both triggers are carried by one requirement because they are alternative conditions on one response, the entry to Standby; INCOSE R20 forbids combining two responses, not two trigger conditions. Release of brake force on this transition is bounded by ACC-SYS-SAF-024.</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-RATIONALE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ISO 15622:2018 cl. 6.3.1; PROJECT-CHOICE:systems-engineer">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SOURCE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-VERIFICATION-TAG</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-VT-SECONDARY</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-VERIFICATION-METHOD</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-VM-TEST</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="brake_pedal_switch [bool]; cancel_switch [bool]; acc_state [enum]">
              <DEFINITION>
