        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_7c3d7fed-9cfd-5c38-b7ab-59860de75ab8" LONG-NAME="ACC-SYS-PRF-003" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ACC-SYS-PRF-003">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-ID</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="Minimum steady-state clearance">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-CHAPTER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-CH-PERFORMANCE</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>While the ACC system is in the Active-Follow state or the Active-Hold state under steady-state conditions, the ACC system shall maintain a clearance to the target vehicle of not less than the greater of 2,5 m and the product of the selected time gap setting and the subject vehicle speed.</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-TEXT</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-EARS-PATTERN</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-EARS-STATEDRIVEN</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-SYSTEM-STATES</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-FOLLOW</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-HOLD</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>ISO 15622:2018 cl. 6.2.3.1 gives the minimum steady-state clearance as MAX(c_min, tau_min times v) and states that the clearance may temporarily fall below that value under transient conditions, after which the system shall adjust the clearance to attain the desired clearance. The relation is read verbatim from the publisher-hosted 2018 preview and is VERIFIED-PRIMARY, but the standard defines c_min as a symbol in cl. 4 without setting a numeric value, so the 2,5 m standstill clearance is project-owned; the requirement therefore carries the weaker DERIVED tag because its weakest constituent is a project choice. 2,5 m is chosen as a bumper-to-bumper clearance that keeps a stopped subject vehicle outside the crush zone of the target vehicle and leaves room for creep on a gradient. The same floor governs the Active-Hold state, which is why ACC-SYS-FUN-005 refers to this requirement for the held clearance. Owned by the systems engineer, 2026-08-18.</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-RATIONALE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ISO 15622:2018 cl. 6.2.3.1; PROJECT-CHOICE:systems-engineer">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SOURCE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-VERIFICATION-TAG</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-VT-DERIVED</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-VERIFICATION-METHOD</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-VM-TEST</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="d_clearance [m]; tau_gap [s]; v_ego [m/s]">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-MEASURAND</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-STATUS</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-STAT-DRAFT</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="1.0">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-REVISION</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="F3, F4">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-FIGURE-REFS</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ACC-SYS-PRF-001, ACC-SYS-FUN-005, ACC-SYS-FUN-021">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-RELATED-REQS</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-VERIFIED-BY</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
          </VALUES>
          <TYPE>
            <SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>ST-ACC-SYS-REQ</SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>
          </TYPE>
        </SPEC-OBJECT>
        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_4814500c-17d7-52c0-b031-5ea51a850c2b" LONG-NAME="ACC-SYS-PRF-020" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ACC-SYS-PRF-020">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-ID</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="Automatic deceleration limit">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-CHAPTER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-CH-PERFORMANCE</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>While the ACC system is in the Active-Cruise state or the Active-Follow state, the ACC system shall limit the automatic deceleration of the subject vehicle to a 2 s moving average of not more than 3,5 m/s².</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-TEXT</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-EARS-PATTERN</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-EARS-STATEDRIVEN</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-SYSTEM-STATES</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-CRUISE</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-FOLLOW</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>Engineering assumption, not a confirmed 2018 value. The limit lives in ISO 15622 cl. 6.4, Operational limits. The clause exists in the 2018 third edition and its title is confirmed from the publisher-hosted preview, but the preview truncates in cl. 6.2.3 and never reaches cl. 6.4, so the 2018 value could not be read from any primary source. The value of 3,5 m/s² over 2 s is verbatim from the 2010 second edition obtained through an unauthorised full-text copy and corroborated by two independent secondary summaries. The value is known to be volatile: the 1999 ISO/DIS set 3,0 m/s², relaxed to 3,5 m/s² by publication. This requirement therefore ships tagged UNVERIFIED-2018; obtaining ISO 15622:2018 cl. 6.4 and confirming the value is an open action in the assumptions register. Jerk is specified separately by ACC-SYS-PRF-021 because INCOSE R19 forbids combining the two. The transient authority ceiling that bounds this comfort limit is ACC-SYS-SAF-040.</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-RATIONALE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ISO 15622:2010 cl. 6.4">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-SOURCE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-VERIFICATION-TAG</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-VT-UNVERIFIED2018</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-VERIFICATION-METHOD</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-VM-TEST</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="a_x_ego [m/s^2]">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-MEASURAND</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-STATUS</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-STAT-DRAFT</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="1.0">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-REVISION</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="F4, F6">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-FIGURE-REFS</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ACC-SYS-PRF-021, ACC-SYS-PRF-022, ACC-SYS-SAF-040">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-RELATED-REQS</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-VERIFIED-BY</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
          </VALUES>
          <TYPE>
            <SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>ST-ACC-SYS-REQ</SPEC-OBJECT-TYPE-REF>
          </TYPE>
        </SPEC-OBJECT>
        <SPEC-OBJECT IDENTIFIER="_250140b9-4b40-5655-b185-b69f0c312249" LONG-NAME="ACC-SYS-PRF-021" LAST-CHANGE="2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00">
          <VALUES>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="ACC-SYS-PRF-021">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-ID</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING THE-VALUE="Automatic negative jerk limit">
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>AD-TITLE</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-STRING-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-STRING>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-CHAPTER</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-CH-PERFORMANCE</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>While the ACC system is in the Active-Cruise state or the Active-Follow state, the ACC system shall limit the rate of increase of automatic deceleration of the subject vehicle to a 1 s moving average of not more than 2,5 m/s³.</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>AD-TEXT</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-XHTML-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-EARS-PATTERN</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-EARS-STATEDRIVEN</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
              <DEFINITION>
                <ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>AD-SYSTEM-STATES</ATTRIBUTE-DEFINITION-ENUMERATION-REF>
              </DEFINITION>
              <VALUES>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-CRUISE</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
                <ENUM-VALUE-REF>EV-ST-ACTIVE-FOLLOW</ENUM-VALUE-REF>
              </VALUES>
            </ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-ENUMERATION>
            <ATTRIBUTE-VALUE-XHTML>
              <THE-VALUE>
                <xhtml:div>
                  <xhtml:p>Engineering assumption, not a confirmed 2018 value. The limit lives in ISO 15622 cl. 6.4, Operational limits, which exists in the 2018 third edition but is past the truncation point of the publisher-hosted preview. The value of 2,5 m/s³ averaged over 1 s is verbatim from the 2010 second edition via an unauthorised full-text copy and is identical in the 1999 ISO/DIS, which is the one clause-6.4 value that did not move between the draft and the published second edition; that stability raises confidence but does not make the 2018 value primary-verified. The requirement is therefore tagged UNVERIFIED-2018. Deceleration magnitude is specified separately by ACC-SYS-PRF-020 because INCOSE R19 forbids combining the two.</xhtml:p>
                </xhtml:div>
              </THE-VALUE>
              <DEFINITION>
